==Production==
The show's executive producers included Alan Fine, Simon Philips, and Eric Rollman, with [[Joe Quesada]] and [[Stan Lee]] as co-executive producers. Cort Lane was supervising producer. [[Mitch Schauer]], creator of the [[Nickelodeon (TV channel)|Nickelodeon]] series ''[[The Angry Beavers]]'', was the show's supervising director and character designer. [[Matt Wayne]] was the show's story editor and head writer.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harvey |first=James |date=February 17, 2009 |title=First Season Of "The Super Hero Squad Show" Set To Launch Late 2009 On Cartoon Network |url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=207 |access-date=December 8, 2010 |publisher=Marvel.toonzone.net |archive-date=October 16, 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121016040951/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=207 |url-status=live }}</ref> Other writers include Michael Ryan, [[Nicole Dubuc]], Atul Rao, Eugene Son, James Krieg, and Mark Hoffmeier. Singer-songwriter [[Parry Gripp]] composed the theme song.

Marvel executive and writer [[Jeph Loeb]] explained the series as something everyone would like, stating "Marvel Super Heroes have always entertained fans of all ages in our comics, and we're proud to offer an animated series that families can enjoy together. With the most exciting super-powered adventures, [[Discovery Family|The Hub]] can now offer the greatest fun of all—experiencing Marvel for the very first time. So whether you want to fly with Thor, suit up with Iron Man or smash with Hulk, this series has everything your family wants to see from our heroes."<ref name="MTV" />

==Broadcast history==
The show's first season was to debut on [[Cartoon Network]] in the United States on September 19, 2009,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Avila |first=Michael |date=July 25, 2009 |title=SDCC 09 - Marvel Goes for Animated Super-Laughs in HERO UP! |url=http://www.newsarama.com/tv/090725-sdcc09-hero-up.html |access-date=December 8, 2010 |publisher=Newsarama.com |archive-date=June 4, 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110604041410/http://www.newsarama.com/tv/090725-sdcc09-hero-up.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> but aired five days earlier on September 14, 2009. The second season of the series, based on ''[[The Infinity Gauntlet]]'', premiered on October 23, 2010 and stopped being shown on Cartoon Network on February 19, 2011, with episode 40 ("Fate of Destiny!"). Afterward, new episodes aired only on [[Teletoon (Canadian TV channel)|Teletoon]] and were available to purchase on [[iTunes]]. On July 23, 2011, the series returned on Cartoon Network, at a new timeslot of 12:00 pm.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harvey |first=James |title="The Super Hero Squad Show" Cartoon Network, Teletoon July 2011 Schedule |url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=674 |access-date=July 6, 2011 |publisher=Toon Zone |archive-date=October 22, 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121022160832/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=674 |url-status=live }}</ref> Although in the next following weeks no new episodes aired. In September 2011, Cartoon Network announced that ''The Super Hero Squad Show'' would be airing new episodes on weekday mornings at 7:00 am starting Monday, October 3, 2011.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Harvey |first=James |title="The Super Hero Squad Show" Returns To Cartoon Network Starting October 2011 |url=http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=707 |access-date=September 29, 2011 |publisher=Toon Zone |archive-date=October 5, 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111005004716/http://marvel.toonzone.net/news.php?action=fullnews&id=707 |url-status=live }}</ref> The series ended on October 14, 2011. A total of 52 episodes were produced for the show. Hub Network began airing the series on January 30, 2012 as part of their daily weekday line-up and aired on Discovery Family until January 30, 2015.<ref name="MTV">{{Cite web |last=Gordon |first=Jeremy |date=January 12, 2012 |title=Marvel's 'Super Hero Squad Show' Set To Premiere On The Hub Network |url=http://splashpage.mtv.com/2012/01/12/marvels-super-hero-squad/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120115140450/http://splashpage.mtv.com/2012/01/12/marvels-super-hero-squad/ |archive-date=January 15, 2012 |access-date=January 14, 2012 |website=[[MTV]]}}</ref><ref name="Hub">{{Cite web |date=January 12, 2012 |title=Super Hero Squad Show Heading to the Hub |url=http://marvel.com/news/story/17940/super_hero_squad_show_heading_to_the_hub |access-date=January 12, 2012 |publisher=Marvel.com |archive-date=June 30, 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120630013017/http://marvel.com/news/story/17940/super_hero_squad_show_heading_to_the_hub |url-status=dead }}</ref> As a result of Cartoon Network losing the rights to the show, all ''Super Hero Squad'' content was removed from the network's website as the result, the rights reverted back from [[Warner Bros. Discovery]] to [[Disney]] following the acquisition of [[Marvel Entertainment]] in 2009. On January 3, 2020, both seasons of the show were added to [[Disney+]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Siegal |first=Jacob |date=January 1, 2020 |title=Everything new coming to Disney+ in January 2020 |url=https://bgr.com/2020/01/01/disney-plus-new-shows-movies-january-2020/ |access-date=October 3, 2021 |publisher=Bgr.com |archive-date=April 12, 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210412043750/https://bgr.com/2020/01/01/disney-plus-new-shows-movies-january-2020/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

The series first premiered on [[Teletoon]] in Canada on Sunday, September 13, 2009, at 8:30 am as part of the network's Action Force block. The show returned on Teletoon on Sunday, February 6, 2011, at 7:00 am for the debut of the second season. All 52 episodes aired in Canada, ending on July 10, 2011.

The series premiered on December 4, 2009, in Australia, on [[ABC3]], in October 2009.

It was aired on [[Nicktoons (British and Irish TV channel)|Nicktoons]] in the UK.<ref>{{Cite web |last=DeMott |first=Rick |date=July 9, 2009 |title=Nick UK Joins Super Hero Squad |url=http://news.awn.com/index.php?ltype=top&newsitem_no=28393 |access-date=December 8, 2010 |publisher=News.awn.com |archive-date=July 12, 2009 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090712205444/http://news.awn.com/index.php?ltype=top&newsitem_no=28393 |url-status=live }}</ref>
The show also used to air reruns on [[Disney XD]] in the United States.

