===Comic books===
{{main|Marvel Super Hero Squad (comics)}}
A four-part comic book series based on the show called ''Marvel Super Hero Squad'' was released in the fall of 2009. The series was a success and Marvel renewed the series in January 2010 as an ongoing series, now entitled: ''Super Hero Squad''. The comic does not feature only characters from the show, but also characters outside the show. As of December 8, 2010, ''Super Hero Squad'' had a total of 12 issues released. No new issues have been released since, seemingly indicating that the comic book franchise has been cancelled. Trying to bring back the franchise, Marvel released a ''Super Hero Squad Spectacular'' where the [[Beyonder]] sends them to another planet with their [[Lethal Legion]] foes.

===Video games===

* ''[[Marvel Super Hero Squad (video game)|Marvel Super Hero Squad]]'' was released on October 20, 2009. 
* ''[[Marvel Super Hero Squad: The Infinity Gauntlet]]'' was released on November 16, 2010. 
* ''[[Marvel Super Hero Squad Online]]'', a [[massively multiplayer online game]], was released to the public in April 2011. The game was heavily based on the ''Super Hero Squad'' franchise, with ''The Super Hero Squad Show'''s character designs returning.<ref>{{Cite web |date=December 14, 2010 |title=Super Hero Squad Online - The Marvel Super Hero MMO for Everyone! |url=http://www.heroup.com |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110311092707/http://www.heroup.com/ |archive-date=March 11, 2011 |access-date=April 2, 2011 |publisher=Heroup.com}}</ref> The game was shut down in 2017.<ref>{{Cite web |date=May 13, 2010 |title=Marvel Super Hero Squad Online Unveiled |url=https://www.shacknews.com/article/63788/marvel-super-hero-squad-online |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201027094110/https://www.shacknews.com/article/63788/marvel-super-hero-squad-online |archive-date=October 27, 2020 |access-date=October 3, 2021 |publisher=Shacknews}}</ref>

===Miscellaneous===
* In the ''[[Mad (TV series)|Mad]]'' segment "Avenger Time", Iron Man, Captain America, Hulk, and Thor enter a reality from the [[Cosmic Cube]] that resembles ''The Super Hero Squad Show''.
* In the ''[[Ultimate Spider-Man (TV series)|Ultimate Spider-Man]]'' episode "Flight of the Iron Spider", [[Living Laser]] is transported to ''The Super Hero Squad Show'' universe, where Thor defeats him.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sims |first=David |date=April 22, 2012 |title=Ultimate Spider-Man: "Flight Of The Iron Spider" |url=https://www.avclub.com/ultimate-spider-man-flight-of-the-iron-spider-1798172500 |access-date=November 29, 2016 |publisher=[[The A.V. Club]] |archive-date=November 29, 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161129144532/http://www.avclub.com/tvclub/ultimate-spider-man-flight-of-the-iron-spider-72643 |url-status=live }}</ref>

